---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageMeta from '@/components/PageMeta.astro';
import GatewayCard from '@/components/ia/GatewayCard.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="PDTF schema and supporting material"
  description="The existing Digital Property Pack JSON Schema, its terminology, implementation guidance and attributed usage evidence."
>
  <PageMeta category="PDTF schema" variant="info" updated="Schema package v3.5.0 · supporting material status varies" />
  <h1>PDTF schema and supporting material</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    This is the implementation-facing PDTF schema material: the JSON Schemas and
    overlays, data dictionary, business glossary, implementation guidance and
    attributed evidence of use. It documents a schema-led exchange contract, not an
    OPDA-endorsed scheme.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--key">
    <p class="callout__label">One family, different evidence states</p>
    <p>
      The v3.5.0 JSON Schema package is the published technical implementation.
      Supporting terminology, guidance, pilots and evidence keep the status shown on
      their own pages; this category neither promotes every record to the same authority
      nor claims endorsement of a scheme.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="use-the-schema">Use and inspect the schema</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <GatewayCard href="/pdtf-schema/schema-and-supporting-material/schema" title="JSON Schemas and overlays" eyebrow="Published implementation" description="Browse the transaction structure, aggregates, overlays and cross-cutting schema views." />
    <GatewayCard href="/pdtf-schema/schema-and-supporting-material/data-dictionary" title="Data dictionary" eyebrow="Source terminology" description="Inspect the schema-derived field catalogue and its recorded definitions." />
    <GatewayCard href="/pdtf-schema/schema-and-supporting-material/business-glossary" title="Business glossary" eyebrow="Source terminology" description="Browse the business concepts and language used by the PDTF schema corpus." />
    <GatewayCard href="/pdtf-schema/schema-and-supporting-material/implementation" title="Implementation guidance" eyebrow="For implementers" description="Start quickly, compose schemas, validate transactions and work with verified claims." />
    <GatewayCard href="/pdtf-schema/schema-and-supporting-material/adoption" title="Usage and implementation evidence" eyebrow="Attributed evidence" description="Review implementations, pilots and programme evidence without treating them as OPDA scheme endorsement or SPDTF adoption." />
  </div>

  <h2 id="relationship">How this relates to the schema-derived ontology</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/pdtf-schema/schema-derived-ontology">ontology derived from the PDTF schema</a> was
    derived from this schema-led corpus. The JSON tree remains useful for
    implementation compatibility and traceability, but its nesting does not by itself
    establish the identities and relationships used in future SPDTF modelling.
  </p>
</Layout>
